#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../ (Memory management) / Retained Edge Counting

    **REC is a physical representation, not source semantics.** Moth has no source-visible reference counting, and no program can name, observe or request a counter.

    REC covers one narrow case: an allocation family whose persistent retained edges are only counted at runtime, disappear independently, and cannot be reclaimed precisely enough through affine last-use analysis, inferred cleanup-frontier regions, field-sensitive splitting or explicit groups. Accepted design with implementation deferred.
]

#[section, reference_content]
